{"name":"Gold Buff","hex":"#ecc481","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gold","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heavy yellow elemental metal of great value, with atomic number 79.","A coin or coinage made of this material, or supposedly so."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["☉ (alchemy)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gold"},{"term":"buff","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Undyed leather from the skin of buffalo or similar animals.","A tool, often one covered with buff leather, used for polishing."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of the color of buff leather, a brownish yellow.","Unusually muscular."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buff"}],"entries":[{"title":"Buff (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Buff is a light brownish yellow, ochreous colour, typical of buff leather. Buff is a mixture of yellow ochre and white: two parts of white lead and one part of yellow ochre produces a good buff, or white lead may be tinted with French ochre alone."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Chamois-natural.jpg/330px-Chamois-natural.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buff_(colour)","wikidata":"Q2085487"},{"title":"Gold","blocks":[{"text":"Gold is a chemical element; its chemical symbol is Au and atomic number 79. In its pure form, it is a bright-metallic-yellow, dense, soft, malleable, and ductile metal. Chemically, gold is a transition metal, a group 11 element, and one of the noble metals. It is one of the least reactive chemical elements, being the second lowest in the reactivity series, with only platinum ranked as less reactive. Gold is solid under standard conditions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Gold-crystals.jpg/330px-Gold-crystals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold","wikidata":"Q897"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Standard_Buff.jpg/250px-Standard_Buff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ea/Standard_Buff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Standard_Buff.jpg/250px-Standard_Buff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Buff after A. Maerz[9]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStandard_Buff.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Buff_after_R._Ridgway.jpg/330px-Buff_after_R._Ridgway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Buff_after_R._Ridgway.jpg/330px-Buff_after_R._Ridgway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Buff after R. Ridgway.[11]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABuff_after_R._Ridgway.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Sand_Drawings.JPG/250px-Sand_Drawings.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Sand_Drawings.JPG/500px-Sand_Drawings.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Sand_Drawings.JPG/250px-Sand_Drawings.JPG?utm_source=en